:S6_31 a dm:StoryCase ;
    dm:storyId "S6-31" ; dm:storySection "6.4.4" ; dm:storyKind "example" ;
    dm:pageSays "Funding the staggered testamentary lead trusts with discounted partnership units and a higher payout gives similar deductions and a GST-free unitrust layer after twelve years." ;
    dm:citesAuthority "2642(a); 2642(e) (notes); Brownstone v. U.S. (2d Cir. 2006) listed" ;
    dm:pageOutcome dm:Allow ; dm:storyScope dm:GradedByModel ; dm:storyGift :S6_31_gift ;
    dm:gapNote "No check models partnership valuation discounts in testamentary lead trusts or GST timing for annuity layers." ;
    dm:pageAccuracyNote "The notes say the narrative's payout rate differs from the worksheets, the annuity layers' GST timing is not shown, and such discounts draw scrutiny." .
# Encodes the 12-year unitrust layer: estate deduction about 65 percent of its funding.
# Not encoded, for counsel: at 65 percent this layer is over the 4947(b)(3)(A) 60 percent
# line, so if the partnership is a family-controlled operating business (not 95 percent
# passive), 4943 applies and a 12-year hold outruns the 5-year (plus 5) bequest window.
:S6_31_gift a dm:PlannedGift ;
    dm:giftVehicle dm:FamilyLeadTrust ; dm:deductionAllowed true ; dm:deductionFor dm:IncomeInterest ;
    dm:incomeInterestForm dm:UnitrustInterest ; dm:charitableIncomeValuePercent "65"^^xsd:decimal ;
    dm:leadBeneficiary :PublicCharity .

